Sounds cool, but let me just add a few notes:

"attack" - On the next (tameness - 5) turns. So the pet would remember 
the command for longer if it were tamer, and if it were close to going 
wild it would ignore you totally.

"heel" - For (1d5* (tameness - 5)) turns... etc.

"play dead" - For (tameness - 5) turns, the pet appears to be a corpse 
and monsters will not attack it (unless they have infravision, etc). The 
DevTeam might even add a "possum" monster that would exhibit this 
behavior without being commanded to do so.

Commanding a pet decreases its tameness by 1, unless it is a "d" of any 
kind (pack instinct) or you are a wizard. At tameness 1, commanding a 
pet will no longer cause a drop in tameness.

